[-] hype		<-->	n++[--0]	./haɪp/
 /haɪp/\
[uncountable] (informal, disapproving)
	;sự thổi phồng, quảng cáo -- (1) advertisements and discussion in the media telling the public about a product and about how good or important it is
		;marketing/media hype
		;Don't believe all the hype—the book isn't that good.
		;Extra Examples:
		;The movie failed to live up to all the hype.
		;This new game is getting plenty of hype.
		;the hype surrounding her latest book
				;Oxford Collocations Dictionary
				;adjective
				;mediamarketingpre-fight…
				;verb + hype
				;live up togetbelieve…
				;hype + verb
				;surround something
				;preposition
				;hype about
		;See full entry
		;Word Origin
	;;












[-] hype		<-->	verb++[--0]	./haɪp/
 /haɪp/
(informal, disapproving)
	;thổi phồng, quảng cáo, tuyên truyền -- (1) to advertise something a lot and make its good qualities seem better than they actually are, in order to get a lot of public attention for it
		;hype something This week his much-hyped new movie opens in London.
		;hype something up The meeting was hyped up in the media as an important event.
		;Word Origin
	;;












[-] outpace		<-->	verb++[--0]	./ˌaʊtˈpeɪs/
 /ˌaʊtˈpeɪs/ [dw]
	;vượt qua -- (1) outpace somebody/something to go, rise, improve, etc. faster than somebody/something
		;synonym outstrip
		;<< outstrip, outpace, >>
		;He easily outpaced the other runners.
		;Demand is outpacing production.
		;Market growth has continued to outpace expectations.
		;Oxford Collocations Dictionary
	;;












